{"step_index":3358,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-22T17:15:37Z","thinking":"Analyzing the provided code snippet suggests it focuses on parallel file processing using `ThreadPoolExecutor`. The function `_process_single_file` hints at handling individual files, likely extracting information or performing transformations. The snippet's core design appears to involve splitting the processing of multiple files across threads for increased efficiency.\n\n\nProcessing a file involves checking its extension to determine the appropriate handler for extracting information. Different handlers exist for Excel, PDF, and JSON files. If the extension isn't supported, processing fails. The process is wrapped in a try-except block to handle potential exceptions during file processing and return an error.\n\n\nThe code leverages a thread pool to process multiple files concurrently, significantly reducing overall processing time. Each file is submitted as a separate task to the executor, enabling simultaneous uploads and processing. Error handling is included to ensure that failures in processing one file do not halt the entire operation. The final result is aggregated into a dictionary containing items extracted from each processed file.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"replace_file_content","args":{"AllowMultiple":false,"Description":"Add ThreadPoolExecutor parallel processing in file_handler.py","EndLine":58,"Instruction":"Implement parallel file processing in read_input_files","ReplacementContent":"from concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor, as_completed\n\n\ndef _process_single_file(\n    filepath: Path,\n    api_key: str | None,\n    base_url: str,\n    gemini_api_key: str | None,\n    profile: str\n) -> tuple[str, list[dict]]:\n    filepath = Path(filepath)\n    ext = filepath.suffix.lower()\n    print(f\"\\n  -> [START] Processing file: {filepath.name} (Type: {ext})\")\n    try:\n        if ext in _EXCEL_EXTENSIONS:\n            items = _process_excel_file(filepath)\n        elif ext in _PDF_EXTENSIONS:\n            items = _process_pdf_file(filepath, api_key, base_url, gemini_api_key, profile)\n        elif ext in _JSON_EXTENSIONS:\n            items = _process_json_file(filepath)\n        else:\n            print(f\"[!] Unsupported extension: {ext} for {filepath.name}\")\n            return filepath.name, []\n\n        print(f\"  -> [DONE] {filepath.name}: {len(items)} items extracted.\")\n        return filepath.name, items\n    except Exception as e:\n        print(f\"[!] Exception processing {filepath.name}: {e}\")\n        return filepath.name, []\n\n\ndef read_input_files(\n    filepaths: list[Path],\n    role: str,\n    api_key: str | None = None,\n    base_url: str = \"https://transform.unstructured.io\",\n    gemini_api_key: str | None = None,\n    profile: str = \"balanced\",\n) -> dict[str, list[dict]]:\n    role_label = \"Shortages\" if role == \"shortages\" else \"Warehouse\"\n    print(f\"\\n{'='*60}\")\n    print(f\"[*] Processing {role_label} files ({len(filepaths)} file(s)) [PARALLEL WORKERS]\")\n    print(f\"{'='*60}\")\n\n    results: dict[str, list[dict]] = {}\n\n    if not filepaths:\n        return results\n\n    if len(filepaths) == 1:\n        fname, items = _process_single_file(filepaths[0], api_key, base_url, gemini_api_key, profile)\n        results[fname] = items\n    else:\n        # Run in parallel across worker threads\n        max_workers = min(len(filepaths), 8)\n        with ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=max_workers) as executor:\n            futures = {\n                executor.submit(_process_single_file, fp, api_key, base_url, gemini_api_key, profile): Path(fp).name\n                for fp in filepaths\n            }\n            for future in as_completed(futures):\n                fname = futures[future]\n                try:\n                    name, items = future.result()\n                    results[name] = items\n                except E