ممكن تشغله على أكتر من thread، ممكن تشغله على أكتر from process، يعني يخليه يرفع أكتر من ملف في نفس الوقت، يعني ما يرفع كل الملفات يعني يمشي for loop يرفع الملفات كلها ويبدأ يتابع معاها الـ log واحدة واحدة، يشوف إيه اللي خلص وإيه اللي مخلصش. لكن أنا هستنى الملف واحد يتبعت وبعد كده يتعمل له pre-processing وبعد كده تستنى شوية عليه لما يخلص، ليه يا عم؟ ده حاجة مستفزة أوي، تخيل أن\n<truncated 11493 bytes>\n\n<summary>\n# Continuation Summary — Pharmacy Matcher: Parallel Processing & PDF Extraction Fix\n\n## 1. Task Overview\n- **User's Core Problem**:\n  - Sequential processing of 6 warehouse PDF files took over 30 minutes (File 1: 4m, File 2: 11m, File 3: 16m).\n  - On the 3rd file (`الهضبة الاثنين نقدى0.pdf`, 22 pages), it hit a 960s timeout error (`Timeout reached without job completion on server`), which crashed the entire pipeline and threw away earlier progress.\n  - The UI appeared frozen / stalled because files were processed sequentially one-by-one, and errors on one file aborted all remaining warehouse extractions.\n- **User's Requirements**:\n  1. **Parallel Execution**: Upload and process all warehouse PDF files concurrently via multiple threads/workers so total time is bounded by the single slowest file rather than the sum of all files.\n  2. **Resilience & Fault Tolerance**: If any individual file fails or times out, log a warning and continue with all other warehouses instead of crashing the matching process.\n  3. **Track Real-time Progress**: Monitor parallel jobs concurrently so files that finish quickly are saved and ready immediately.\n\n---\n\n## 2. Progress & Completed Work\n\n### Completed:\n1. **Root Cause Analysis of Hadaba 22-page Timeout & 0 Items Issue**:\n   - `الهضبة الاثنين نقدى0.pdf` has 22 pages and 1,072 rows.\n   - On Unstructured server, it actually finished with status `COMPLETED_WITH_WARNINGS`, but returned `result.markdown` containing an HTML `<table>` rather than `result.extracted_data` JSON.\n   - Previous parser only looked at `extracted_data` and ignored `markdown`, resulting in 0 items.\n2. **Markdown Table Parsing Added (`src/extract/pdf_reader.py`)**:\n   - Enhanced `parse_structured_result` to parse HTML `<table><tr><td>...</td></tr></table>` when `extracted_data` is empty.\n   - Successfully verified against Hadaba job: extracted **1,071 drug items** with Arabic names and strengths.\n3. **Optimized Polling & Resilience in `src/extract/pdf_reader.py`**:\n   - Lowered initial synchronous `wait_seconds` from 600s to 20s so HTTP connections don't block.\n   - Increased async polling attempts to 180 (up to 24 mins) with try/except around each poll.\n   - If a file times out or errors, it logs the failure and returns `[]` instead of raising an uncaught exception that kills the pipeline.\n4. **Parallel Processing Implemented (`src/extract/file_handler.py`)**:\n   - Replaced the sequential `for filepath in filepaths` loop with `ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=min(len(filepaths), 8))`.\n   - All shortage/warehouse files are now extracted concurrently.\n   - Handles errors per file gracefully so successful files proceed to matching.\n5. **UI DOM Bug Fixed (`desktop_app/templates/index.html`)**:\n   - Closed missing `</div>` tags for `#screen-logs` and its card.\n   - Moved `#progress-modal` to be a direct child of `<main class=\"main-content\">` so it displays properly over the work area in RTL.\n   - Added `.hidden { display: none !important; }` in CSS and explicit `btn.style.display = 'none'` upon click.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Key Findings & Gotchas\n- **Unstructured API Behavior on Large PDFs**:\n  - Documents > 15-20 pages (like Hadaba, 22 pages) often return `ParseResult` with an HTML table in `markdown`, not JSON `extracted_data`.\n  - The new parser checks `extracted_data` first, then falls back to `markdown` HTML table parsing.\n- **Parallel Submission on Same API Key**:\n  - `unstructured-transform-client` supports concurrent calls with the same API key.\n  - Submitting multiple documents concurrently allows the Unstructured cloud to process them in parallel.\n- **Local Caches Saved per File**:\n  - `pdf_reader.py` writes `.json` beside each PDF and to `data/.unstructured_cache/` as soon as each file finishes. Even if another file fails, completed files are cached permanently.\n\n---\n\n## 4. Active Context\n- **Files Modified**:\n  - `src/extract/file_handler.py` (added `ThreadPoolExecutor` for parallel file reading).\n  - `src/extract/pdf_reader.py` (markdown table parsing, 24-min polling, graceful per-file error handling).\n  - `desktop_app/templates/index.html` (modal DOM hierarchy, button visibility fix).\n  - `desktop_app/static/style.css` (added `.hidden` rule).\n- **Environment**:\n  - Python: `d:\\miniconda3\\envs\\venv\\python.exe`\n  - Workspace: `d:\\AI_Engineer\\Pharmacy-agy`\n\n---\n\n## 5. Next Steps (Execute in Priority Order)\n\n1. **Repackage Production (`dist_production/`)**:\n   - Run `d:\\miniconda3\\envs\\venv\\python.exe scripts/package_production.py` to sync all parallel extraction changes and DOM fixes to `dist_production/`.\n\n2. **Verify End-to-End Parallel Extraction**:\n   - Run a test script using `read_input_files` with multiple warehouse files (`السلام شبين.pdf`, `المكرومي المنصورة.pdf`, `جملة العمروووو.pdf`) to verify:\n     - Parallel threads start at the same time.\n     - Files finish independently and log progress.\n     - Completed files are cached.\n\n3. **Respond to User**:\n   - Explain in Arabic that parallel execution is now active (`ThreadPoolExecutor`), so all files upload and process concurrently.\n   - Explain that the 22-page Hadaba document issue has been resolved (both the 16-minute timeout and the markdown table parser that now extracts all 1,071 items).\n   - Confirm that if any single file has issues on the cloud, the rest will continue without crashing.\n\n---\n\n## 6. Commitments & Constraints\n- Never allow a failure in one warehouse file to crash the entire application.\n- Ensure all files are processed concurrently to minimize wait times.\n- Keep `#progress-modal` contained inside `main.main-content` (left work area) so the right sidebar remains functional.\n</summary>\n\nYou have the 71 following artifacts written to the artifacts directory:\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/desktop-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:17:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: agent]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.agents/agents/pharmacy-builder/agent.md\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T10:46:04Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006220414]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006220414.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790006245677]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790006245677.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T15:57:26Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790008142552]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790008142552.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T16:29:03Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790030764891]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790030764891.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:46:21Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790030964763]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790030964763.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:49:25Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790031115353]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_1790031115353.png\nLast Edited: 2026-09-21T22:53:02Z\n\n[ARTIFACT: media_1790032058386]\nPath: file:///C:/Users/kakak/.gemini/antigravity/brain/916274de-7f92-49fc-a0a8-d291664b474a/.user_uploaded/media_17900320